# cook_app colors

Widgets take color from the theme. `AppColors` swatches (`green1`, `amber1`, `hint`, `brandGreen`, …) exist to build `ColorScheme` and `AppExtraColors`. Do not paint widgets with those swatches.

```dart
final scheme = Theme.of(context).colorScheme;
final extra = AppExtraColors.of(context);

// primaryContainer is green1. secondaryContainer is amber1.
decoration: BoxDecoration(color: scheme.primaryContainer)
color: extra.hint
backgroundColor: Theme.of(context).scaffoldBackgroundColor
```

`AppColors` in a widget is only for a color that has no role, such as the character fill `coral1`. Page background is `scaffoldBackgroundColor`. Sidebar surface is `AppExtraColors.sidebar`.

If a new color is a role (container, accent, label, surface), add it to `ColorScheme` or `AppExtraColors` in `ui/core/themes/colors.dart`, then read it from the theme.
